+# Performance history
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+On a synthetic 5,000-record store, the end-to-end `SessionStart` hook cost was:
+
+| Read path | p50 |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Before `PRAGMA quick_check` was removed from the read path | 16.608 ms |
+| After `quick_check` was moved off the read path | 1.063 ms |
+
+These are measured values from 300 hook invocations per configuration using the
+release build and `muninn-bench perf --records 5000 --cues 15000 --runs 300`.
+The measurement includes process startup through hook exit. The before
+configuration ran the live health checks: `quick_check`, the FTS row count, and
+the body-length query. In the after configuration, the hook reads the recorded
+`quick_check` result and the trigger-maintained `fts_rows` counter; the body
+limit is enforced by a schema `CHECK`. The `fts_rows` counter and body `CHECK`
+were introduced as part of the same read-path change, so the p50 difference is
+for that combined change rather than for `quick_check` in isolation.
